# Codebase Safety Rules

## Files You Must NEVER Modify (unless the ticket explicitly says to)

These are frozen contracts. Changing them breaks downstream consumers:

- `types/command.ts` — Command type shape
- `services/mcp/types.ts` — MCP protocol types
- `utils/sessionStorage.ts` lines 139-156 — `isTranscriptMessage`, `isChainParticipant`

## Functions You Must NEVER Change Signatures Of

- `resolveHookPermissionDecision` in `services/tools/toolHooks.ts`
- `permissionComponentForTool` in `components/permissions/PermissionRequest.tsx`
- `query` generator in `query.ts`
- `buildSystemPromptBlocks` in `services/api/claude.ts`

You can call these functions differently, wrap them, or add code before/after them. But do not change their parameter types, return types, or behavior.

## Patterns You Must Follow

When adding to `AppState`: put new fields outside `DeepImmutable<{}>`, after the `tasks` field.

When adding to `Entry` union: also add the else-if branch in `loadTranscriptFile` AND extend the return value.

When adding hook events: update all 5 sites atomically (see enhancement-engineering rule, Section 4).

When adding feature-gated code to existing files: use a self-contained if-block, never restructure surrounding code.

## Import Rules

- Use `import type` for type-only imports (prevents runtime dependency when feature is disabled)
- Use dynamic `import()` or conditional `require()` for feature-gated heavy modules
- Never add top-level imports for feature-gated modules in non-gated files
